@prefix tmk:     <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/> .
@prefix tmkc:    <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/examination>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "TM-Knowledge — examination module"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment """Who does what, and to what.

The process classes (application, examination, objection, outcome) stay declared
and unpopulated: no application data is in scope, and an examination outcome is
one thing the system never states (CLAUDE.md §2).

The role classes are populated with definitions. The reviewer's covering note
(`review/returned/260826-expert-feedback.md`, HANDOFF Q17) named nine terms that
needed high-level definitions — Registrar, Delegate, Examiner, Decision Maker,
Office Practice, Subject Matter Expert, Oppositions, Grounds for Rejection,
Adverse Report — because the seed vocabulary was drawn from Part 29 alone. On
2026-10-08 the owner approved the ontology review's role model (C1 to C6) and
the restructuring below (C5, ADR-0123); each of the nine now has a concept in
the vocabulary, and each role a class here."""@en-AU ;
    owl:imports <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> ;
    owl:versionInfo "draft — not approved" .

tmk:TradeMarkApplication a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Trade mark application"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "UNPOPULATED. The thing being examined. No application data exists in this programme and none is in scope."@en-AU .

tmk:Examination a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Examination"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "UNPOPULATED. The process applied to an application."@en-AU .

tmk:Objection a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Objection"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "UNPOPULATED. A ground raised against an application in an examination."@en-AU .

tmk:ExaminationOutcome a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Examination outcome"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment """UNPOPULATED, and it must stay that way for this pilot.

Deciding an examination outcome is explicitly out of scope (CLAUDE.md §6), and
the prohibited-use set exists to keep it there: PU-0001 and PU-0002 are the two
outputs that state one."""@en-AU .

# --- roles: who acts, and with what power (review C5, ADR-0123) -------------
#
# Until 2026-10-08 these were six flat sibling classes, each "UNDEFINED —
# HANDOFF Q17", although Q17 was answered (ADR-0074) and authoring has been
# allowed since ADR-0079. The owner confirmed the review's summary of the roles
# and their power structure ("a correct and accurate interpretation") and
# approved restructuring them (C5). Every comment below is machine-written and
# unreviewed, and rests on the provision or passage it names.
#
# A tmk:Role is somebody who acts. The vocabulary's concept of that role — the
# term "examiner" as an entry — is a tmk:ProcessRole in legal-concepts.ttl, and
# the two are kept apart on purpose (ADR-0098 c2). tmk:roleConcept bridges them,
# from each class to the concept that names it. Who holds power over whom is not here but on the edges between role
# concepts — holdsDelegationFrom, exercisesPowersOf, actsUnderDirectionOf,
# consults, escalatesTo, reviewsDecisionsOf, hearsAppealsFrom, requiresConsentOf,
# prevailsOver, actsUnderControlOf (relations.ttl), each carrying the sentence
# that grounds it.

tmk:Role a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Role"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A person, office or body acting in the trade marks system. The families below sort roles by where their power comes from, and are disjoint where that matters: an office is not a delegate, and neither is a party."@en-AU .

tmk:roleConcept a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "role concept"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "From a role class to the vocabulary concept (a tmk:ProcessRole) that names it — the bridge the review found missing (C5). An annotation, so it licenses no inference: the concept does not become a role, and the role does not become a term. Stated on the class, so no concept node gains a statement outside its store's graph. Machine-written, unreviewed (ADR-0123)."@en-AU .

# offices: created by the Act itself

tmk:Office a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Role ;
    rdfs:label "Office"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A statutory office the Act creates and whose powers it confers directly."@en-AU .

tmk:Registrar a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0046 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Office ;
    rdfs:label "Registrar"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment """The Registrar of Trade Marks (s 201). The Act gives the Registrar the powers and functions it confers, and the Registrar may delegate them by signed instrument (s 206).

Load-bearing for CLAUDE.md rule 5: the Manual states the Registrar's practice and does not bind this office's discretion. The office decides through delegates, but a delegate is not the Registrar (owner's rulings C1, C2)."""@en-AU .

tmk:DeputyRegistrar a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0159 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Office ;
    rdfs:label "Deputy Registrar"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A Deputy Registrar of Trade Marks (s 205): has all the Registrar's powers and functions except delegation, subject to the Registrar's directions, and an act of a Deputy Registrar is taken to be the Registrar's. The power comes by statute, not by instrument — which is what separates this office from a delegate."@en-AU .

# delegates: power by instrument

tmk:Delegate a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0171 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Role ;
    rdfs:label "Delegate"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "An employee holding the Registrar's powers by signed instrument (s 206(1)), who may be required to act under the Registrar's direction or supervision (s 206(2)). A delegate's decision is made under the Registrar's powers; the delegate is not the Registrar."@en-AU .

tmk:Examiner a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0044 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Delegate ;
    rdfs:label "Examiner"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "An APS 5 examiner, one of the delegates currently authorised to accept applications (Part 18.2.2.2). At examination, the decision maker."@en-AU .

tmk:SeniorExaminer a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0174 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Delegate ;
    rdfs:label "Senior examiner"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "An APS6 senior examiner, delegated to accept (Part 18.2.2.2); between examiner and examination team leader in the chain of command (owner's ruling C6)."@en-AU .

tmk:TeamLeader a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0173 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Delegate ;
    rdfs:label "Examination team leader"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "An EL1 examination team leader, delegated to accept (Part 18.2.2.2) and holding powers examiners do not — notifying a proposed revocation of acceptance (Part 38.1.1.3), most section 65A amendments (Part 9.4.4.7.1). The first point of escalation (C6)."@en-AU .

tmk:HearingOfficer a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0172 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Delegate ;
    rdfs:label "Hearing Officer"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A delegate in the Oppositions and Hearings Section who conducts hearings and decides contested matters, acting under delegation from the Registrar (Part 52.2)."@en-AU .

# advisers: consulted, never deciding

tmk:AdvisoryRole a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Role ;
    rdfs:label "Advisory role"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "Somebody a delegate consults when unsure of the correct decision; the delegate still decides (owner's ruling C6)."@en-AU .

tmk:SubjectMatterExpert a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0175 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:AdvisoryRole ;
    rdfs:label "Subject matter expert"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A delegate with expertise in a particular matter — classification, a language, Indigenous knowledge — whom another delegate consults (Parts 10.4.4.1.3, 14.4.4.1.2, 30.3.3.4.1)."@en-AU .

# parties and their representatives

tmk:Party a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Role ;
    rdfs:label "Party"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A person whose rights an application, registration or proceeding concerns — who applies, opposes, owns or holds. Not a decision maker in it."@en-AU .

tmk:Applicant a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0116 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Party ;
    rdfs:label "Applicant"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The person in whose name an application is for the time being proceeding (s 6)."@en-AU .

tmk:Opponent a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0117 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Party ;
    rdfs:label "Opponent"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A person who opposes registration by filing a notice of opposition (s 52)."@en-AU .

tmk:RegisteredOwner a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0084 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Party ;
    rdfs:label "Registered owner"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The person in whose name a trade mark is registered (s 6)."@en-AU .

tmk:AuthorisedUser a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0083 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Party ;
    rdfs:label "Authorised user"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A person who uses a trade mark under the control of its owner (s 8(1)). Treated differently from the owner in most contexts, and never the same entity (owner's ruling A4)."@en-AU .

tmk:Holder a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0132 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Party ;
    rdfs:label "Holder of an international registration"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The person in whose name an international registration is recorded in the International Register (reg 17A.2)."@en-AU .

tmk:Representative a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Role ;
    rdfs:label "Representative"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "Somebody who acts for a party — a registered trade marks attorney or a lawyer. Not a party, and not a decision maker."@en-AU .

tmk:TradeMarkAttorney a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0178 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Representative ;
    rdfs:label "Trade marks attorney"@en-AU .

# bodies outside the office

tmk:ReviewBody a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Role ;
    rdfs:label "Review body"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A tribunal or court that reviews, or hears appeals from, the Registrar's decisions."@en-AU .

tmk:AdministrativeReviewTribunal a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0134 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:ReviewBody ;
    rdfs:label "Administrative Review Tribunal"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "Reviews certain decisions of the Registrar on their merits, standing in the shoes of the original decision maker (Part 52.5.5.2). Its decisions are administrative, not judicial (review C7)."@en-AU .

tmk:PrescribedCourt a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0139 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:ReviewBody ;
    rdfs:label "Prescribed court"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2), which hear appeals from the Registrar's decisions (ss 35, 56, 190)."@en-AU .

tmk:CoRegulator a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Role ;
    rdfs:label "Co-regulator"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A body outside the office whose consent or certificate a step needs."@en-AU .

tmk:Commission a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0133 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:CoRegulator ;
    rdfs:label "Australian Competition and Consumer Commission"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "Assesses the rules of a certification trade mark, and its consent is needed to assign a registered one (ss 175, 180)."@en-AU .

tmk:InternationalBody a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Role ;
    rdfs:label "International body"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A body of the Madrid system."@en-AU .

tmk:InternationalBureau a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0138 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:InternationalBody ;
    rdfs:label "International Bureau"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "Keeps the International Register; in a classification dispute on a Madrid export application its opinion stands over the Office of origin's (Part 14.2.2.2.2)."@en-AU .

tmk:OfficeOfOrigin a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0136 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:InternationalBody ;
    rdfs:label "Office of origin"@en-AU .

tmk:Office owl:disjointWith tmk:Delegate , tmk:Party , tmk:Representative .
tmk:Delegate owl:disjointWith tmk:Party , tmk:Representative .
tmk:Party owl:disjointWith tmk:Representative .

# --- decision maker: a role in a decision, not a peer of examiner -----------

tmk:DecisionMaker a owl:Class ;
    tmk:roleConcept tmkc:GC-0045 ; rdfs:subClassOf tmk:Role ;
    rdfs:label "Decision maker"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment """Whoever a decision is decided by — a role somebody plays in a decision, not a kind of person beside the examiner (review C5). At examination the examiner is the decision maker; after a hearing, the Hearing Officer or Deputy Registrar; on review, the Tribunal, standing in the shoes of the original one. The Manual calls the Registrar and the deciding delegate "an administrative decision maker" (Parts 2.3.2.3.2, 46.2).

It matters for the presumption of registrability: the bar is the decision maker's satisfaction that a ground exists, and a model that equates the role with one office loses who that is (GE-0010, GE-0047)."""@en-AU .

tmk:decidedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range tmk:DecisionMaker ;
    rdfs:label "decided by"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "From a decision to whoever made it. Its range is what makes someone a decision maker: being the one a decision was decided by."@en-AU .

# tmk:constrainsRole was declared here with rdfs:range tmk:Role. It is now a
# defined predicate in the relation dictionary (relations.ttl, ADR-0123), used
# between concepts — a rule and the role concept it governs — and a range of
# tmk:Role would have made every role concept a role, the merge ADR-0098 c2 forbids.
